# CADDY_TLS_MODE=internal: Caddy's own private CA, for an install with neither a
# public DNS name nor an enterprise PKI. Caddy issues and renews the certificate
# itself. Clients must trust its root, which lives in the atlas-mcp-tls-data volume
# at /data/caddy/pki/authorities/local/root.crt. Copy that file (it is a public
# certificate, not a key) to each client and point ATLAS_CA_BUNDLE /
# backendTLS.root / NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS at it.
tls internal
